# Track A Phase 2C (H-1 remediation): narrow exceptions for the specific
# workbooks that are durable independent-DCF-validation EVIDENCE, not raw or
# interim data pulls -- the general *.xlsx rule above is for financial data
# pulls, which these are not. Each file is the frozen, hashed record that a
# genuine reconciliation was run (or, for the archive, that one genuinely
# failed and why) -- see docs/independent-validation-plan.md and
# validation/dcf_reconciliation/history/phase2b_initial_no_go/README.md.
# Leaving them git-ignored would let that record silently disappear on a
# `git clean` or a fresh clone, with no history to recover it from. Listed
# by exact path only -- this does NOT re-enable *.xlsx generally, and no
# other workbook in the repository is exempted.
# (independent_dcf_validation.xlsx, V1, is already tracked from a prior
# force-add and needs no exception here; it is listed in the three
# artifacts' own documentation for context.)
!/validation/dcf_reconciliation/dcf_reconciliation.xlsx
!/validation/dcf_reconciliation/history/phase2b_initial_no_go/dcf_reconciliation.xlsx
!/validation/independent_dcf/independent_dcf_validation_v2.xlsx

# Logs
*.log
